24	116,868,365,1224 - 80,1183,240,1230	Fig. 24.	The lower part of the winged seed-vessel of Red Maple, cut away at its base to show the seed lying in its place.
25	86,1186,232,1388	Fig. 25.	The Red Maple seed a little magnified, with the coats cut away to show the embryo coiled up inside and filling it completely.
26	170,1412,385,1616 - 200,1575,244,1610	Fig. 26.	The embryo taken out and a little unfolded: the two seed-leaves partly crumpled together above, the radicle or stemlet curving away below.
27	426,1208,765,1626	Fig. 27.	The embryo straightened out after throwing off the seed-coats: two rather thick, strap-shaped seed-leaves spreading in a V on top of a long stemlet.
